  nodeAbstract: 
  nodeTextLayers:
  - When a GTP activates the G Alpha subunit of GProtein, G Alpha and the G Beta
    Gamma dimer disassociate and both are freed to leave the GLP1-R.
  - After one complex of GProtein leaves an activated GLP1-R, another GProtein complex
    can come by and bind in the same location.
